@startuml examination_status_state_diagram
title Examination Status Lifecycle (domain_model.md §5, §7, §9)

state draft
state planned
state completed
state cancelled
state missed

[*] --> draft
[*] --> planned
[*] --> completed
[*] --> cancelled
[*] --> missed

draft <--> planned
draft <--> completed
draft <--> cancelled
draft <--> missed
planned <--> completed
planned <--> cancelled
planned <--> missed
completed <--> cancelled
completed <--> missed
cancelled <--> missed

draft --> [*] : delete
planned --> [*] : delete
completed --> [*] : delete
cancelled --> [*] : delete
missed --> [*] : delete

note top of draft
  Every create/update validates the COMPLETE
  resulting record, not the submitted diff. Any
  status may transition to any other status via
  update, provided the resulting record satisfies
  its status-dependent required fields below. No
  further transition matrix is defined
  (domain_model.md §9) — do not add restrictions
  without an approved decision.

  draft: title only
  planned / cancelled / missed: + scheduled_date
  completed: + completed_date (<= today)
end note

state planned {
  [*] --> upcoming
  upcoming --> overdue : scheduled_date/time passes
  note right of overdue
    Derived at query/presentation time from
    status + scheduled_date + scheduled_time +
    the user's local time. Never persisted
    (domain_model.md §7). Only "planned"
    examinations can be upcoming or overdue.
  end note
}

note right of planned
  Reminder: may be created, updated, or
  reactivated only while planned. Leaving
  planned deactivates it (not deleted);
  returning to planned does NOT auto-reactivate
  it.

  RecurrenceRule: create/modify only while
  planned; the rule itself persists unchanged
  across every status change.
end note

note bottom of draft
  Drafts are excluded from upcoming, overdue,
  and calendar results regardless of which
  optional fields happen to be filled in.
end note

@enduml
